  "classification": {
    "words": "Each GRADED_DISAGREED account-day is classified from its persisted columns alone. With V the market value, F the external flow, p the holdings price return and V0 the same account's market value on the previous trading day: NO_PRIOR when there is no previous-day row, the previous value is null or not above zero, or V, F or p is null. Otherwise the account's return v = V/V0 - 1 and its flow share s = |F|/V0 are compared with the date's own tolerance tau: FLOW when s is above tau and |v - p| is not, VALUE when |v - p| is above tau and s is not, FLOW_AND_VALUE when both are above, NEITHER when neither is. The label says which input disagrees in persisted terms; it is inferred, not read from the producer's internal comparison.",
    "claim": "inferred"
  },
